<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patraos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 335–315 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Patraus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patraos was a king of Paeonia from about 335 to 315 BCE, during the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>, whose overlordship he accepted. He issued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> tetradrachms showing a Paeonian horseman spearing a fallen enemy, a design that underlines the kingdom's cavalry tradition. He was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audoleon">Audoleon</a>.</p></div>
